  {
   "id": 549299,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose that States K and L annex State M and increase the house size proportionately.\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li>Determine the new house size, <span data-math=\"m\">m</span>, that is necessary.</li>\n<li>Calculate the standard divisor based on the new house size.</li>\n<li>Use the Hamilton method to reapportion the seats.</li>\n<li>Does the new-states paradox occur?</li>\n</ol>",
